# .b2b-secrets — the datacenter's secrets, KEY=VALUE, one per line.
#
#   cp .b2b-secrets.example .b2b-secrets && chmod 600 .b2b-secrets
#
# born2root.toml is tracked and its tests fail on a literal credential, so
# nothing secret goes there. This file is read with sed by setup/host/dc_lib.sh
# (never sourced), must be mode 600, and is ignored by git (`*secret*`). It
# never enters the ISO: every value travels to the guest over SSH after the
# build, which is why a rebuilt VM needs nothing but this file to come back.
#
# TS_AUTHKEY        Tailscale auth key from https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
#                   Generate it REUSABLE + EPHEMERAL + PRE-APPROVED: reusable so a
#                   rebuilt VM can log in with the same file (a one-off key is spent
#                   by the first VM and `make tailscale` then fails), ephemeral so
#                   the old VM vanishes from the tailnet when it is destroyed.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD   the backup repository password. `make backup` mints one when
#                   absent. Copy it to a password manager: every snapshot on
#                   sgoinfre is noise without it.
# BAAS_API_KEY      the grobase tenant key `make seed` and client apps use;
#                   `make tenant_key` writes it (and BAAS_API_KEY_<TENANT>).
#                   Restoring a backup brings the same key back.
# CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN   cloudflared tunnel token, only once a domain exists.
TS_AUTHKEY=
RESTIC_PASSWORD=
BAAS_API_KEY=
CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
